## What Makes Tesla Lemon Law Claims Unique?

Tesla lemon law claims come with a few complications that make these cases different from traditional gas-powered lemons.

## 1. Software Updates

Tesla frequently releases over-the-air updates that are supposed to fix bugs. But in many cases, these updates introduce new problems or fail to resolve the issue long-term. It creates a moving target for repair attempts.

## 2. Service Delays

Unlike traditional automakers with a widespread dealer network, Tesla operates a limited number of service centers. Wait times for diagnostics or repairs can stretch for weeks or longer, depending on your location.

In some cases, Tesla may cancel appointments, mark issues as resolved without documentation, or push software updates in place of hands-on repairs. These delays make it harder to reach the minimum number of repair attempts required for a lemon claim.

## 3. No Dealership Network

Tesla [sells directly to consumers](https://www.investopedia.com/articles/active-trading/072115/what-makes-teslas-business-model-different.asp), so there’s no dealership network to step in and help. You’re mostly left to communicate through the Tesla app, which is notorious for giving vague responses.

Additionally, it may take repeated follow-ups or legal pressure to get written records, service notes, or formal defect reports.

None of these issues can prevent you from filing a claim. But they do make it easier for Tesla to stall or avoid responsibility. That’s why it helps to work with a Tesla lemon law lawyer who knows exactly how the company operates and how to build a strong case.

## What Can You Recover Under Tesla Lemon Law?

If your Tesla is deemed a lemon under CA lemon law, you may be entitled to a repurchase (also called a lemon law buyback), including:

- Your down payment

- Monthly payments made to date

- Payoff of your car loan or lease

- Registration and taxes

- Incidental costs (towing, rental, etc.)

The manufacturer may subtract a small mileage offset based on how long the car worked correctly before the defect showed up. However, a skilled Tesla lemon law attorney will make sure this deduction is calculated fairly.

Alternatively, you may be offered a replacement vehicle with the same specs. You’ll also be reimbursed for registration and other fees associated with the defective vehicle.

In both cases, Tesla will also cover your attorney’s fees. You do not have to pay out-of-pocket for legal representation.

